# Print the input backwards.
#
# Uses the slide instructions ( and ) to walk along the tape, storing one
# character per cell, so it works for input of any length up to the tape size.
# A finite-width program can do this only because it can slide.
,    # read the first character
?    # while it is not end of input (0)
)    #   slide right onto a fresh cell
,    #   read the next character into it
:    # loop
(    # step back onto the last character
?    # while the cell is not the zero to the left of the first character
.    #   print it
(    #   slide left
:    # loop
